# Project

antistrefo is a static-analysis CLI and MCP server. No debugger. The only persistent store is the per-binary `<binary>.asdb` sidecar written by the deep pass (mapped, versioned, SHA-256 keyed).

    antistrefo <command> [args]
    antistrefo mcp

The product name is antistrefo. C symbols stay `re_` and macros `RE_`. That prefix is a link-time guard against Capstone and zlib. Do not rename it to match the product.

- Executable `antistrefo.exe`. JSON schema id `antistrefo/1`. License MIT.
- Core is C11 (`src/utils`, `src/features`). Shell is C++17 (`src/cli`, `src/mcp`).
- ASCII only in code: no smart quotes, em dashes, or arrows. Box drawing goes in as byte escapes (`"\xe2\x94\x80"`).
- LF, one final newline, no trailing whitespace, no tabs. Indent 4 spaces. K&R braces. Column limit 100.
- File cap 500 lines. Function body cap 60 lines and 4 nesting levels.
- Names: `re_` prefix, `snake_case`, `_t` for types.
- Canonical rulebook: `.rules/rules.md`. The gate is `scripts/check.py`.
